# Electron / electron-builder binary mirrors.
#
# npm PACKAGES resolve from the public registry (see the repository-root .npmrc).
# But these tools download their own BINARIES from GitHub at install/build time,
# which some corporate networks block:
#   - electron            -> electron-v<ver>-<platform>-<arch>.zip   (postinstall)
#   - electron-builder    -> winCodeSign, nsis, app-builder-bin      (at build time)
#
# If your network cannot reach github.com, point these at your own mirror of the
# GitHub release assets. Prefer setting them as environment variables rather than
# committing site-specific URLs to the repository.
#
# ── Electron runtime binary ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# electron_mirror=https://<your-mirror-host>/repository/electron/
# electron_custom_dir={{ version }}
#
# ── electron-builder helper binaries ───────────────────────────────────────
# electron_builder_binaries_mirror=https://<your-mirror-host>/repository/electron-builder-binaries/
